lowing long-term in vitro exposure of <italic toggle="yes">Macaca mulatta</italic> trophoblast stem cells to biologically relevant levels of endocrine disruptors</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name name-style="western"><surname>Midic</surname><given-names initials="U">Uros</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="A1">1</xref></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name name-style="western"><surname>Goheen</surname><given-names initials="B">Benjamin</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="A1">1</xref></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name name-style="western"><surname>Vincent</surname><given-names initials="KA">Kailey A.</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="A1">1</xref></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name name-style="western"><surname>VandeVoort</surname><given-names initials="CA">Catherine A</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="A2">2</xref></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name name-style="western"><surname>Latham</surname><given-names initials="KE">Keith E.</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="A1">1</xref><xref rid="FN1" ref-type="author-notes">3</xref></contrib></contrib-group><aff id="A1">
